# ===========================================================================
#  Build context exclusions
#  .containerignore and .dockerignore are kept byte-identical so that podman
#  and docker see exactly the same context; each engine reads only its own
#  file, and a difference between the two would show up as a build that works
#  under one and not the other.
#
#  The Containerfile COPYs nothing. Every file this repository ships -
#  setup-dotFiles.sh, bashrc, tmux.conf, fzf.bash, yay-apps.txt - is
#  bind-mounted at /app when the container runs, precisely so that editing one
#  does not mean rebuilding an image. Shipping the working tree as build
#  context would buy nothing and cost a copy of .git/ on every build, which is
#  larger than everything else here put together.
#
#  So the context is emptied wholesale. Re-open it by exception, one `!` line
#  per file, if a COPY ever genuinely needs something.
# ===========================================================================

*

# The build file itself, so `-f Containerfile .` keeps working on engines that
# resolve it through the context rather than reading it directly.
!Containerfile
